  "rationale": "With no defences, exfiltration is reachable: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. Then pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. So at least one control is needed. Every exfiltrate technique needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Those need a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, all of which require stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin comes only from dump_dbadmin_dc or dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which come only from auth_dc and auth_adfs, both requiring NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore cuts every path to exfiltration, so the minimum is 1."
